            %p
              This follows from Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InSpectraHomotopyFiberSequencesAreHomotopyCofiberSequences"}
              by the fact that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"} Spectra
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#TheStableHomotopyCategoryIsAdditive"}> this Prop.
              ).
            %p
              See also
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.04773"} arXiv:1906.04773, Prop. 6.2.11
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/132347/381"} MO:q/132347
            %p
            .num_remark
              %h6 Remark
              %p
                This property of Spectra (Prop.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InSpectraHomotopyFiberSequencesAreHomotopyCofiberSequences"}
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyPullbacksOfSpectraAreHomotopyPushouts"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} stable (∞,1)-categories
                (see
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "stable+infinity-category#Definition"} there
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+derivators"} stable derivators
                (see
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "stable+derivator#Definition"} there
          %h3#monoidal_structure Monoidal structure
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                With the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi whe
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(L_{whe}Top_*)
                becomes a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} algebra object
                    in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mi whe
                          %msub
                            %mi Top
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(L_{whe}Top_*)
                    with respect to this monoidal structure is an
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+ring+spectrum"} associative ring spectrum
                %li
                  %p
                    a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} commutative algebra object
                    in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mi whe
                          %msub
                            %mi Top
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(L_{whe}Top_*)
                    with respect to this monoidal structure is a
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring+spectrum"} commutative ring spectrum
          %h3#prime_spectrum_and_morava_ktheory Prime spectrum and Morava K-theory
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+spectrum+of+a+monoidal+stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} prime spectrum of a monoidal stable (∞,1)-category
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-localization"} p-local
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+spectra"} finite spectra
            is labeled by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+K-theories"} Morava K-theories
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thick+subcategory+theorem"} thick subcategory theorem
          %h3#model_category_presentation Model category presentation
          %p
            There are several
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentations
            of the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories+of+spectra"} model categories of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+categories"} monoidal model categories
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
            is presented by an ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+rings"} A-∞ rings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-modules"} ∞-modules
            are presented by 1-categorical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+objects"} monoid objects
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+objects"} module objects
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brave+new+algebra"} brave new algebra
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+spectra"}> model structure on spectra
            ,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectrum"}> symmetric spectrum
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+symmetric+spectra"} model structure on symmetric spectra
            %li
              %p
